<title>SWEDEN: Sandvik 1996 profit by business area.</title>
<headline>Sandvik 1996 profit by business area.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a breakdown of Swedish engineer Sandvik AB's 1996 results by business area. For 1996 Sandvik posted a 21 percent fall in profit after financial items to 4.45 billion crowns. (Profit after depreciation, Mln SKR)</p>
<p>					  1996	   1995</p>
<p> Sandvik Tooling		   2,031	  2,436</p>
<p> Sandvik Rock Tools		  220	    219</p>
<p> Sandvik Hard Materials	    133	    185</p>
<p> Sandvik Steel		     1,203	  1,623</p>
<p> Sandvik Saws and Tools	    161	    184</p>
<p> Sandvik Process Systems	   -24	    101</p>
<p> Seco Tools			    402	    542</p>
<p> Group activities		    -17	    -96</p>
<p> TOTAL				 4,109	  5,194</p>
<p>Operating profit before depreciation was negatively affected by the stronger Swedish crown by 600 million crowns, the company said. The profit fell to 5.27 billion crowns from 6.27 billion.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
